course: dictionary
lesson: 14093
title: Thin, skin-like parts
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Membranous is a science word. It describes something made of a membrane, which is a thin, soft layer like skin that covers or separates parts of a living thing. «The bat's wings are membranous.» A bat's wing is thin skin stretched over long bones, so membranous means thin and skin-like.
explain: Use the clues around the word. «The dragonfly's membranous wings shone in the sun.» Wings that shine in the sun are thin enough to let the light through, so membranous fits. Test your meaning in the sentence: thin, skin-like wings shone in the sun. It makes sense.
explain: Scientists use this word for thin layers in plants and animals, such as the skin inside an eggshell. It is a formal word, so you will meet it mostly in science books. Break it into parts: membrane plus -ous, meaning like a membrane.
fact: A membrane is a thin, soft layer, like skin.
fact: Membranous means made of a membrane, or like one.
fact: «Membranous wings» are thin, skin-like wings, such as a bat's or an insect's.
fact: Inside an eggshell there is a thin, membranous layer.
fact: Membranes also surround the cells of living things.
exercise: «The bat's membranous wings were stretched between its long fingers.» What does membranous mean here? | *Thin and skin-like | Sharp and pointed | Bright and coloured like a flower | Heavy and made of metal
exercise: «Inside the eggshell is a thin, membranous layer.» Which word in this sentence is a clue that membranous means thin? | layer | eggshell | inside | *thin
exercise: Which of these has membranous wings? | A rock | A stone wall | A hard metal drum | *A bat
test: «Membranous» most likely describes which thing? | A thick wooden door | A heavy stone block | A bright electric lamp | *A thin, skin-like layer
test: Sam says membranous means fast. Why is he wrong? | It means noisy | It means round and hard | It means very fast | *It means thin and skin-like
exam: A membrane is best described as: | A kind of sweet | A loud sound | *A thin, soft layer like skin | A hard shell of bone
